{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_968c1c6cdc6545a6ad6a38b1","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 1330 lines\n1: (ns yang.python.antlr.prelude\n2:   \"The Python runtime profile, written as Universal AST\n3:    (docs/design/yang.antlr.md §8.1, §8.2, §9.3). Python semantics for\n4:    operators, truthiness, equality, objects, exceptions and escapes live\n5:    here as guest code, not in Clojure: the lowering only emits applications\n6:    of these names.\n7: \n8:    Value encoding:\n9:      int             host integer (untagged)\n10:      float           {:py/float x}: tagged on every host, because JS cannot\n11:                      tell 2 from 2.0 (owner decision 3)\n12:      bool            host true / false (numeric as 1 / 0)\n13:      None            :py/None\n14:      str             {:py/str \\\"...\\\"}\n15:      list            a cell holding {:py/type :list :items [...]}\n16:      dict            a cell holding {:py/type :dict :index {nkey slot}\n17:                      :keys [...] :vals [...]}: insertion order is the keys\n18:                      vector, never a host map's order; keys are normalized\n19:                      so 1, 1.0 and True are one key\n20:      set             a cell holding {:py/type :set :index {nkey slot}\n21:                      :keys [...]}: insertion order, keys normalized as for\n22:                      dicts\n23:      function        a cell holding {:py/type :function :name s :spec spec\n24:                      :defaults [...] :kwdefaults [[name v] ...]\n25:                      :code (fn [args] ...)}; identity is the cell ref\n26:      class           a cell holding {:py/type :class :name s :base cls\n27:                      :attrs {name value}}\n28:      instance        a cell holding {:py/type :instance :class cls\n29:                      :attrs {name value}}\n30:      bound method    {:py/type :method :self obj :fn function}\n31:      tuple           {:py/type :tuple :items [...]}: a value; hashable when\n32:                      its elements are\n33:      slice           {:py/type :slice :start a :stop b :step c}\n34:      range           {:py/type :range :start a :stop b :step s}\n35:      module globals  a dict (owner decision 1): the module body receives it\n36:                      as `%globals` and every function closes over it, which\n37:                      is Python's own `__globals__`; a miss is NameError\n38: \n39:    Calling convention: a function's `:code` takes one vector of arguments\n40:    laid out as the parameters are written. `py/call-kw` (and `py/call`,\n41:    its positional-only form) binds positional arguments, keywords, defaults,\n42:    `*args` and `**kwargs` from the function's static spec; every binding\n43:    failure is a Python TypeError.\n44: \n45:    Runtime state is two cells, reached through the store (`yin/def` is\n46:    reserved for the prelude and builtins):\n47:      py.rt/handlers  the handler stack: frames [kind payload rest depth];\n48:                      a :handler frame holds the continuation `raise`\n49:                      delivers to, a :finally frame a thunk every exit\n50:                      through it runs (raise passes the exception, escapes\n51:                      and normal completion pass None); nil when empty\n52:      py.rt/out       the values `print` collected, one vector per call\n53: \n54:    Escapes and handlers tell the first pass through a capture point from a\n55:    re-entry with a flag cell allocated before the capture (`:first`, then\n56:    `:re-entered`): heap writes survive continuation invocation, so the flag\n57:    answers without inspecting the continuation's representation. An escape\n58:    unwinds to the depth it captured, running finally thunks on the way.\n59: \n60:    Integer `//`, `%`, `**`, bitwise operators and float floor have no\n61:    portable host primitive; they are exact algorithms here over + - * <\n62:    (doubling division, binary-descent floor, two's-complement recursion),\n63:    valid within 2^53.\n64: \n65:    Host names the prelude depends on and does not define: `host-names`\n66:    (the cell module from yin.vm.module, the rest from yin.vm.data).\"\n67:   (:require\n68:     [yang.python.antlr.uast :as u]))\n69: \n70: \n71: (def host-names\n72:   \"Module exports the prelude calls.\"\n73:   '#{cell/new cell/get cell/set! data/count data/into data/subvec\n74:      data/str-concat data/str-length data/str-index-of data/str->code-points\n75:      data/code-points->str})\n76: \n77: \n78: (def ^:private core-definitions\n79:   \"Pure definitions: lambdas only, so defining them runs nothing.\"\n80:   '[;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- kinds\n81:     [py/cell? (fn [x] (= (get x :type) :cell-ref))]\n82:     [py/str? (fn [x] (not (nil? (get x :py/str))))]\n83:     [py/str (fn [s] (assoc {} :py/str s))]\n84:     [py/float? (fn [x] (not (nil? (get x :py/float))))]\n85:     [py/float (fn [x] (assoc {} :py/float (* 1.0 x)))]\n86:     [py/tuple (fn [items] (assoc (assoc {} :py/type :tuple) :items items))]\n87:     [py/conj (fn [xs x] (conj xs x))]\n88:     [py/arg (fn [args i] (get args i))]\n89:     [py/numeric?\n90:      (fn [x]\n91:        (if (= x true)\n92:          true\n93:          (if (= x false)\n94:            true\n95:            (if (py/float? x)\n96:              true\n97:              (if (nil? (get x :py/str))\n98:                (if (nil? (get x :type))\n99:                  (if (nil? (get x :py/type))\n100:                    (if (= x :py/None) false (not (= x :py/unbound)))\n101:                    false)\n102:                  false)\n103:                false)))))]\n104:     [py/num\n105:      (fn [x]\n106:        (if (= x true) 1 (if (= x false) 0 (if (py/float? x) (get x :py/float) x))))]\n107:     [py/zero? (fn [x] (let [v (py/num x)] (if (= v 0) true (= v 0.0))))]\n108:     [py/content-type (fn [x] (if (py/cell? x) (get (