{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_a466944338a94f4e8daec0c3","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 740 lines\nNote: showing lines 1-740. More of the file remains. Use offset=741 to continue.\n1: (ns yang.python.antlr.lower\n2:   \"The lowering interpreter: CST packets in, Universal AST program batches\n3:    out (docs/design/yang.antlr.md §3.5, §8.5). Portable.\n4: \n5:    Per packet: validate the tree, analyze scopes (`yang.python.antlr.scope`),\n6:    then lower with one `case` arm per grammar rule. A rule the spike does not\n7:    support fails with `:yang.python.antlr/unsupported` naming the rule and\n8:    construct; a rule with no arm fails with\n9:    `:yang.python.antlr/unhandled-rule`. Nothing is silently dropped.\n10: \n11:    Decided lowering rules (collab/1790795118566 brief):\n12:    - Every function-local binding and every parameter is a cell, allocated\n13:      at function entry: parameters initialised, other locals `:py/unbound`.\n14:      Reads are `py/local-get` (unbound -> UnboundLocalError), writes\n15:      `cell/set!`. Module names and `global` names live in the module's\n16:      namespace dict, `%globals` (`py/global-get`, a miss is NameError;\n17:      `py/global-set`); `yin/def` is reserved for the prelude and builtins.\n18:    - A `def` or `lambda` is a function object (`py/make-function`) whose\n19:      code takes one argument vector; every call is `(py/call f [args])` or,\n20:      with keywords, `(py/call-kw f [args] [[name value] ...])`; the callee\n21:      binds positional, keyword, default, `*args` and `**kwargs`.\n22:    - Control flow is continuations: a function with a `return` runs its body\n23:      under `py/call-ec`; loops are self-applied lambdas whose `break` and\n24:      `continue` are escapes; `try` installs a handler continuation through\n25:      `py/try`, and `raise` invokes the innermost one. `finally` is a\n26:      `py/try-finally` frame that every