only adds when p ≥ 1, and…wait, on JVM p starts as (/ (pow2) 2): pow2-above returns long; (/ long 2) → Ratio for odd case (only when pow2=1? pow2-above y 1: doubles until k > x; returns k, a power of 2 ≥ 2…if y < 1 then…y ≥ 0; for y=0.5: k=1 (>0.5) → (/ 1 2) → Ratio 1/2 → floor-descend with p=1/2 < 1 → immediately returns n=0 ✓ floor(0.5)=0 ✓). Even powers → (/ 8 2) = long 4 ✓. Then in descend (/ p 2): p=1 → 1/2 Ratio → stop ✓. So Ratios appear but comparisons are exact ✓. Result consistent with JS's double p (0.5) ✓ same stopping condition ✓ same n ✓. OK no issue — but wait, does the VM's `/` primitive allow Ratio results, and are subsequent ops portably OK? n only accumulates by adding p when (+ n p) ≤ x; p ≥ 1 there; on JVM p is long ≥1 or a Ratio < 1 (stop). ✓ consistent.\n\nLet me check vm primitives for `*`, `/`, `<` behavior. Grep primitives in vm.cljc.\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Let me verify how the VM's `*` and `/` primitives behave (overflow semantics per host) since the"}]}}
