)` catching each, `isinstance(1, (int, str))`-style with user classes).\n\n- **P2 | prelude.cljc:632-639, 690, 489-496 (over vm.cljc:360-363) | The 2^53 integer bound is documented but unenforced, and crossing it diverges per host.** VM primitives `*`/`+` are host ops: JVM throws `ArithmeticException` (a host error outside guest diagnostics), CLJS doubles go silently inexact above 2^53, CLJD/Dart wraps at 64 bits. Reachable with fully supported syntax: `print(2 ** 53 + 1)` → `…993` on JVM, `…992` on Node; `print(3 ** 40)` → exact on JVM, inexact on Node, wrapped on Dart; `1 << 63` → JVM host crash, Node fine. This breaks the determinism/parity invariant on accepted programs; `py/floor` (prelude.cljc:597-607) already sets the precedent of a uniform guest `OverflowError`. **Fix:** magnitude guards raising guest `Overflow"}]}}
