7"}},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_968c1c6cdc6545a6ad6a38b1","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 1330 lines\n1: (ns yang.python.antlr.prelude\n2:   \"The Python runtime profile, written as Universal AST\n3:    (docs/design/yang.antlr.md §8.1, §8.2, §9.3). Python semantics for\n4:    operators, truthiness, equality, objects, exceptions and escapes live\n5:    here as guest code, not in Clojure: the lowering only emits applications\n6:    of these names.\n7: \n8:    Value encoding:\n9:      int             host integer (untagged)\n10:      float           {:py/float x}: tagged on every host, because JS cannot\n11:                      tell 2 from 2.0 (owner decision 3)\n12:      bool            host true / false (numeric as 1 / 0)\n13:      None            :py/None\n14:      str             {:py/str \\\"...\\\"}\n15:      list            a cell holding {:py/type :list :items [...]}\n16:      dict            a cell holding {:py/type :dict :index {nkey slot}\n17:                      :keys [...] :vals [...]}: insertion order is the keys\n18:                      vector, never a host map's order; keys are normalized\n19:                      so 1, 1.0 and True are one key\n20:      set             a cell holding {:py/type :set :index {nkey slot}\n21:                      :keys [...]}: insertion order, keys normalized as for\n22:                      dicts\n23:      function        a cell holding {:py/type :function :name s :spec spec\n24:                      :defaults [...] :kwdefaults [[name v] ...]\n25:                      :code (fn [args] ...)}; identity is the cell ref\n26:      class           a cell holding {:py/type :class :name s :base cls\n27:                      :attrs {name value}}\n28:      instance        a cell holding {:py/type :instance :class cls\n29:                      :attrs {name value}}\n30:      bound method    {:py/type :method :self obj :fn function}\n31:      tuple           {:py/type :tuple :items [...]}: a value; hashable when\n32:                      its elements are\n33:      slice           {:py/type :slice :start a :stop b :step c}\n34:      range           {:py/type :range :start a :stop b :step s}\n35:      module globals  a dict (owner decision 1): the module body receives it\n36:                      as `%globals` and every function closes over it, which\n37:                      is Python's own `__globals__`; a miss is NameError\n38: \n39:    Calling convention: a function's `:code` takes one vector of arguments\n40:    laid out as the parameters are written. `py/call-kw` (and `py/call`,\n41:    its positional-only form) binds positional arguments, keywords, defaults,\n42:    `*args` and `**kwargs` from the function's static spec; every binding\n43:    failure is a Python TypeError.\n44: \n45:    Runtime state is two cells, reached through the store (`yin/def` is\n46:    reserved for the prelude and builtins):\n47:      py.rt/handlers  the handler stack: frames [kind payload rest depth];\n48:                      a :handler frame holds the continuation `raise`\n49:                      delivers to, a :finally frame a thunk every exit\n50:                      through it runs (raise passes the exception, escapes\n51:                      and normal completion pass None); nil when empty\n52:      py.rt/out       the values `print` collected, one vector per call\n53: \n54:    Escapes and handlers tell the first pass through a capture point from a\n55:    re-entry with a flag cell allocated before the capture (`:first`, then\n56:    `:re-entered`): heap writes survive continuation invocation, so the flag\n57:    answers without inspecting the continuation's representation. An escape\n58:    unwinds to the depth it captured, running finally thunks on the way.\n59: \n60:    Integer `//`, `%`, `**`, bitwise operators and float floor have no\n61:    portable host primitive; they are exact algorithms here over + - * <\n62:    (doubling division, binary-descent floor, two's-complement recursion),\n63:    valid within 2^53.\n64: \n65:    Host names the prelude depends on and does not define: `host-names`\n66:    (the cell module from yin.vm.module, the rest from yin.vm.data).\"\n67:   (:require\n68:     [yang.python.antlr.uast :as u]))\n69: \n70: \n71: (def host-names\n72:   \"Module exports the prelude calls.\"\n73:   '#{cell/new cell/get cell/set! data/count data/into data/subvec\n74:      data/str-concat data/str-length data/str-index-of data/str->code-points\n75:      data/code-points->str})\n76: \n77: \n78: (def ^:private core-definitions\n79:   \"Pure definitions: lambdas only, so defining them runs nothing.\"\n80:   '[;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- kinds\n81:     [py/cell? (fn [x] (= (get x :type) :cell-ref))]\n82:     [py/str? (fn [x] (not (nil? (get x :py/str))))]\n83:     [py/str (fn [s] (assoc {} :py/str s))]\n84:     [py/float? (fn [x] (not (nil? (get x :py/float))))]\n85:     [py/float (fn [x] (assoc {} :py/float (* 1.0 x)))]\n86:     [py/tuple (fn [items] (assoc (assoc {} :py/type :tuple) :items items))]\n87:     [py/conj (fn [xs x] (conj xs x))]\n88:     [py/arg (fn [args i] (get args i))]\n89:     [py/numeric?\n90:      (fn [x]\n91:        (if (= x true)\n92:          true\n93:          (if (= x false)\n94:            true\n95:            (if (py/float? x)\n96:              true\n97:              (if (nil? (get x :py/str))\n98:                (if (nil? (get x :type))\n99:                  (if (nil? (get x :py/type))\n100:                    (if (= x :py/None) false (not (= x :py/unbound)))\n101:                    false)\n102:                  false)\n103:                false)))))]\n104:     [py/num\n105:      (fn [x]\n106:        (if (= x true) 1 (if (= x false) 0 (if (py/float? x) (get x :py/float) x))))]\n107:     [py/zero? (fn [x] (let [v (py/num x)] (if (= v 0) true (= v 0.0))))]\n108:     [py/content-type (fn [x] (if (py/cell? x) (get (cell/get x) :py/type) nil))]\n109:     [py/function? (fn [x] (= (py/content-type x) :function))]\n110: \n111:     ;; ---------------------------------------------------------- escapes\n112:     ;; The handler stack is a chain of frames [kind payload rest depth]:\n113:     ;; :handler frames hold the continuation `raise` delivers to, :finally\n114:     ;; frames hold a thunk of one argument (the exception, or None) that\n115:     ;; every exit through them runs. Depth makes \"unwind to here\" an integer\n116:     ;; comparison.\n117:     [py/frame-depth (fn [hs] (if (nil? hs) 0 (get hs 3)))]\n118:     [py/frame\n119:      (fn [kind payload rest]\n120:        (py/conj (py/conj (py/conj (py/conj [] kind) payload) rest)\n121:                 (+ 1 (py/frame-depth rest))))]\n122:     [py/raise\n123:      (fn [e]\n124:        (let [hs (cell/get py.rt/handlers)]\n125:          (if (nil? hs)\n126:            (:py/no-handler e)\n127:            (if (= (get hs 0) :finally)\n128:              (do (cell/set! py.rt/handlers (get hs 2))\n129:                  ((get hs 1) e)\n130:                  (py/raise e))\n131:              ((get hs 1) e)))))]\n132:     [py/unwind-to\n133:      ;; pop frames above depth d, running each finally thunk with None\n134:      (fn [d]\n135:        (let [hs (cell/get py.rt/handlers)]\n136:          (if (nil? hs)\n137:            :py/None\n138:            (if (<= (get hs 3) d)\n139:              :py/None\n140:              (do (cell/set! py.rt/handlers (get hs 2))\n141:                  (if (= (get hs 0) :finally) ((get hs 1) :py/None) :py/None)\n142:                  (py/unwind-to d))))))]\n143:     [py/try\n144:      (fn [body handler orelse]\n145:        (let [saved (cell/get py.rt/handlers)\n146:              flag (cell/new :first)]\n147:          ((fn [r]\n148:             (if (= (cell/get flag) :first)\n149:               (do (cell/set! flag :re-entered)\n150:                   (cell/set! py.rt/handlers (py/frame :handler r saved))\n151:                   (body)\n152:                   (cell/set! py.rt/handlers saved)\n153:                   (orelse))\n154:               (do (cell/set! py.rt/handlers saved)\n155:                   (handler r))))\n156:           (%capture))))]\n157:     [py/try-finally\n158:      ;; normal exit runs `fin` here; raise and escapes run it as they\n159:      ;; unwind through the :finally frame\n160:      (fn [body fin]\n161:        (let [saved (cell/get py.rt/handlers)]\n162:          (do (cell/set! py.rt/handlers (py/frame :finally fin saved))\n163:              (let [v (body)]\n164:                (do (cell/set! py.rt/handlers saved)\n165:                    (fin :py/None)\n166:                    v)))))]\n167:     [py/call-ec\n168:      (fn [f]\n169:        (let [saved (cell/get py.rt/handlers)\n170:              flag (cell/new :first)]\n171:          ((fn [r]\n172:             (if (= (cell/get flag) :first)\n173:               (do (cell/set! flag :re-entered)\n174:                   (f (fn [x]\n175:                        (do (py/unwind-to (py/frame-depth saved))\n176:                            (cell/set! py.rt/handlers saved)\n177:                            (r x)))))\n178:               r))\n179:           (%capture))))]\n180:     [py/type-of\n181:      (fn [x] (if (= (py/content-type x) :instance) (get (cell/get x) :class) :py/None))]\n182:     [py/with\n183:      ;; the language reference's expansion: __exit__ is looked up before\n184:      ;; __enter__ runs; an exception calls __exit__(type, value, None) and\n185:      ;; is suppressed when that is truthy; every other exit calls\n186:      ;; __exit__(None, None, None)\n187:      (fn [mgr suite]\n188:        (let [exit (py/getattr mgr \"__exit__\")\n189:              value (py/call (py/getattr mgr \"__enter__\") [])\n190:              hit (cell/new false)]\n191:          (py/try-finally\n192:            (fn []\n193:              (py/try (fn [] (suite value))\n194:                      (fn [e]\n195:                        (do (cell/set! hit true)\n196:                            (if (py/truthy\n197:                                  (py/call exit\n198:                                           (py/conj (py/conj (py/conj [] (py/type-of e)) e)\n199:                                                    :py/None)))\n200:                              :py/None\n201:                              (py/raise e))))\n202:                      (fn [] :py/None)))\n203:            (fn [x]\n204:              (if (cell/get hit)\n205:                :py/None\n206:                (py/call exit (py/conj (py/conj (py/conj [] :py/None) :py/None)\n207:                                       :py/None)))))))]\n208: \n209:     ;; ---------------------------------------------------------- exceptions\n210:     [py/make-class\n211:      (fn [name base]\n212:        (cell/new (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :py/type :class) :name name)\n213:                                :base base)\n214:                         :attrs {})))]\n215:     [py/make-instance\n216:      (fn [cls]\n217:        (cell/new (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :py/type :instance) :class cls)\n218:                         :attrs {})))]\n219:     [py/make-exc\n220:      (fn [cls msg]\n221:        (let [e (py/make-instance cls)]\n222:          (do (py/setattr e \"args\" (py/tuple (py/conj [] msg))) e)))]\n223:     [py/raise-new (fn [cls msg] (py/raise (py/make-exc cls msg)))]\n224:     [py/type-error (fn [msg] (py/raise-new py.b/TypeError msg))]\n225:     [py/as-exception\n226:      (fn [x]\n227:        (if (= (py/content-type x) :class)\n228:          (py/call x [])\n229:          (if (py/cell? x)\n230:            x\n231:            (py/type-error {:py/str \"exceptions must derive from BaseException\"}))))]\n232:     [py/subclass?\n233:      (fn [c target]\n234:        (if (= c :py/None)\n235:          false\n236:          (if (= c target) true (py/subclass? (get (cell/get c) :base) target))))]\n237:     [py/isinstance\n238:      (fn [o cls]\n239:        (if (= (py/content-type o) :instance)\n240:          (py/subclass? (get (cell/get o) :class) cls)\n241:          false))]\n242: \n243:     ;; ---------------------------------------------------------- names\n244:     [py/local-get\n245:      (fn [c n]\n246:        (let [x (cell/get c)]\n247:          (if (= x :py/unbound)\n248:            (py/raise-new py.b/UnboundLocalError\n249:                          (py/str (data/str-concat\n250:                                    \"cannot access local variable '\" (get n :py/str)\n251:                                    \"' where it is not associated with a value\")))\n252:            x)))]\n253:     [py/global-get\n254:      (fn [g n]\n255:        (let [c (cell/get g)\n256:              slot (get (get c :index) n :py/missing)]\n257:          (if (= slot :py/missing)\n258:            (py/raise-new py.b/NameError\n259:                          (py/str (data/str-concat \"name '\" (get n :py/str)\n260:                                                   \"' is not defined\")))\n261:            (get (get c :vals) slot))))]\n262:     [py/global-set (fn [g n x] (do (py/dict-set g n x) :py/None))]\n263:     [py/global-or\n264:      ;; a builtin name: the module's binding when present, else the builtin\n265:      (fn [g n builtin]\n266:        (let [c (cell/get g)\n267:              slot (get (get c :index) n :py/missing)]\n268:          (if (= slot :py/missing) builtin (get (get c :vals) slot))))]\n269:     [py/class-ns-get\n270:      ;; a name assigned in a class body, read in that body: the class\n271:      ;; namespace as it is now, else `fallback` (globals, then builtins)\n272:      (fn [cls name fallback]\n273:        (let [x (get (get (cell/get cls) :attrs) name :py/missing)]\n274:          (if (= x :py/missing) (fallback) x)))]\n275: \n276:     ;; ---------------------------------------------------------- functions\n277:     ;; A function's `spec` is static data from the lowering:\n278:     ;;   {:params [positional names] :star? bool :kwonly [names] :kwstar? bool}\n279:     ;; `defaults` holds the trailing positional defaults and `kwdefaults`\n280:     ;; [[name value] ...] the keyword-only ones, both evaluated at\n281:     ;; definition time. `code` takes one vector laid out as the parameters\n282:     ;; are written: positional, the *args tuple, keyword-only, the **kwargs\n283:     ;; dict.\n284:     [py/make-function\n285:      (fn [name spec defaults kwdefaults code]\n286:        (cell/new (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :py/type :function)\n287:                                                     :name name)\n288:                                              :spec spec)\n289:                                       :defaults defaults)\n290:                                :kwdefaults kwdefaults)\n291:                         :code code)))]\n292:     [py/fn-error\n293:      (fn [fc msg] (py/type-error (py/str (data/str-concat (get fc :name) msg))))]\n294:     [py/index-of\n295:      (fn [xs x i]\n296:        (let [y (get xs i :py/stop)]\n297:          (if (= y :py/stop) -1 (if (= y x) i (py/index-of xs x (+ i 1))))))]\n298:     [py/pad\n299:      ;; the first n of xs, :py/missing where xs is shorter\n300:      (fn [xs n i acc]\n301:        (if (< i n) (py/pad xs n (+ i 1) (conj acc (get xs i :py/missing))) acc))]\n302:     [py/bind-keyword\n303:      ;; state is [positional-slots kwonly-slots kwargs-dict-or-nil]\n304:      (fn [fc state name x]\n305:        (let [spec (get fc :spec)\n306:              pi (py/index-of (get spec :params) name 0)\n307:              ki (py/index-of (get spec :kwonly) name 0)\n308:              dup (py/str (data/str-concat \"() got multiple values for argument '\"\n309:                                           name \"'\"))]\n310:          (if (< -1 pi)\n311:            (if (= (get (get state 0) pi) :py/missing)\n312:              (assoc state 0 (assoc (get state 0) pi x))\n313:              (py/fn-error fc (get dup :py/str)))\n314:            (if (< -1 ki)\n315:              (if (= (get (get state 1) ki) :py/missing)\n316:                (assoc state 1 (assoc (get state 1) ki x))\n317:                (py/fn-error fc (get dup :py/str)))\n318:              (if (nil? (get state 2))\n319:                (py/fn-error fc (data/str-concat\n320:                                  \"() got an unexpected keyword argument '\" name \"'\"))\n321:                (if (py/dict-has? (get state 2) (py/str name))\n322:                  (py/fn-error fc (get dup :py/str))\n323:                  (do (py/dict-set (get state 2) (py/str name) x) state)))))))]\n324:     [py/bind-keywords\n325:      (fn [fc state kwargs i]\n326:        (let [pair (get kwargs i :py/stop)]\n327:          (if (= pair :py/stop)\n328:            state\n329:            (py/bind-keywords fc (py/bind-keyword fc state (get pair 0) (get pair 1))\n330:                              kwargs (+ i 1)))))]\n331:     [py/fill-defaults\n332:      (fn [fc slots defaults n i]\n333:        (if (< i n)\n334:          (if (= (get slots i) :py/missing)\n335:            (let [j (- i (- n (data/count defaults)))]\n336:              (if (< j 0)\n337:                (py/fn-error fc (data/str-concat\n338:                                  \"() missing required positional argument '\"\n339:                                  (get (get (get fc :spec) :params) i) \"'\"))\n340:                (py/fill-defaults fc (assoc slots i (get defaults j)) defaults n\n341:                                  (+ i 1))))\n342:            (py/fill-defaults fc slots defaults n (+ i 1)))\n343:          slots))]\n344:     [py/lookup-pair\n345:      (fn [pairs name i]\n346:        (let [pair (get pairs i :py/stop)]\n347:          (if (= pair :py/stop)\n348:            :py/missing\n349:            (if (= (get pair 0) name) (get pair 1) (py/lookup-pair pairs name (+ i 1))))))]\n350:     [py/fill-kwdefaults\n351:      (fn [fc slots names i]\n352:        (let [nm (get names i :py/stop)]\n353:          (if (= nm :py/stop)\n354:            slots\n355:            (if (= (get slots i) :py/missing)\n356:              (let [d (py/lookup-pair (get fc :kwdefaults) nm 0)]\n357:                (if (= d :py/missing)\n358:                  (py/fn-error fc (data/str-concat\n359:                                    \"() missing required keyword-only argument '\"\n360:                                    nm \"'\"))\n361:                  (py/fill-kwdefaults fc (assoc slots i d) names (+ i 1))))\n362:              (py/fill-kwdefaults fc slots names (+ i 1))))))]\n363:     [py/bind-args\n364:      ;; positional, then keywords, then defaults; every failure a TypeError\n365:      (fn [fc args kwargs]\n366:        (let [spec (get fc :spec)\n367:              n (data/count (get spec :params))\n368:              given (data/count args)\n369:              star (get spec :star?)]\n370:          (if (if (< n given) (not star) false)\n371:            (py/fn-error fc \"() takes too many positional arguments\")\n372:            (let [state (py/bind-keywords\n373:                          fc\n374:                          (py/conj (py/conj (py/conj [] (py/pad args n 0 []))\n375:                                            (py/pad [] (data/count (get spec :kwonly)) 0 []))\n376:                                   (if (get spec :kwstar?) (py/dict-new) nil))\n377:                          kwargs\n378:                          0)\n379:                  slots (py/fill-defaults fc (get state 0) (get fc :defaults) n 0)\n380:                  ko (py/fill-kwdefaults fc (get state 1) (get spec :kwonly) 0)\n381:                  with-star (if star\n382:                              (py/conj slots\n383:                                       (py/tuple (if (< n given) (data/subvec args n) [])))\n384:                              slots)\n385:                  with-ko (data/into with-star ko)]\n386:              (if (get spec :kwstar?) (py/conj with-ko (get state 2)) with-ko)))))]\n387:     [py/call (fn [f args] (py/call-kw f args []))]\n388:     [py/call-kw\n389:      (fn [f args kwargs]\n390:        (if (= (get f :py/type) :method)\n391:          (py/call-kw (get f :fn) (data/into (py/conj [] (get f :self)) args) kwargs)\n392:          (let [t (py/content-type f)]\n393:            (if (= t :function)\n394:              (let [fc (cell/get f)] ((get fc :code) (py/bind-args fc args kwargs)))\n395:              (if (= t :class)\n396:                (py/instantiate f args kwargs)\n397:                (py/type-error {:py/str \"object is not callable\"}))))))]\n398:     [py/instantiate\n399:      (fn [cls args kwargs]\n400:        (let [inst (py/make-instance cls)\n401:              init (py/class-lookup cls \"__init__\")]\n402:          (do (if (= init :py/missing)\n403:                (py/setattr inst \"args\" (py/tuple args))\n404:                (py/call-kw init (data/into (py/conj [] inst) args) kwargs))\n405:              inst)))]\n406:     [py/extend\n407:      ;; call-site *iterable and display *iterable\n408:      (fn [acc it] (data/into acc (py/to-vector it)))]\n409:     [py/kw-extend\n410:      ;; call-site **mapping: its string keys become keyword pairs\n411:      (fn [acc d]\n412:        (if (= (py/content-type d) :dict)\n413:          (py/kw-pairs acc (get (cell/get d) :keys) (get (cell/get d) :vals) 0)\n414:          (py/type-error {:py/str \"argument after ** must be a mapping\"})))]\n415:     [py/kw-pairs\n416:      (fn [acc ks vs i]\n417:        (let [k (get ks i :py/stop)]\n418:          (if (= k :py/stop)\n419:            acc\n420:            (if (py/str? k)\n421:              (py/kw-pairs (conj acc (conj (conj [] (get k :py/str)) (get vs i))) ks vs\n422:                           (+ i 1))\n423:              (py/type-error {:py/str \"keywords must be strings\"})))))]\n424: \n425:     ;; ---------------------------------------------------------- attributes\n426:     [py/class-lookup\n427:      (fn [cls name]\n428:        (if (= cls :py/None)\n429:          :py/missing\n430:          (let [c (cell/get cls)\n431:                found (get (get c :attrs) name :py/missing)]\n432:            (if (= found :py/missing)\n433:              (py/class-lookup (get c :base) name)\n434:              found))))]\n435:     [py/method\n436:      (fn [o f] (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :py/type :method) :self o) :fn f))]\n437:     [py/bind (fn [o m] (if (py/function? m) (py/method o m) m))]\n438:     [py/attr-error (fn [name] (py/raise-new py.b/AttributeError (py/str name)))]\n439:     [py/getattr\n440:      (fn [o name]\n441:        (if (py/cell? o)\n442:          (let [c (cell/get o)\n443:                t (get c :py/type)]\n444:            (if (= t :instance)\n445:              (let [own (get (get c :attrs) name :py/missing)]\n446:                (if (= own :py/missing)\n447:                  (let [m (py/class-lookup (get c :class) name)]\n448:                    (if (= m :py/missing) (py/attr-error name) (py/bind o m)))\n449:                  own))\n450:              (if (= t :class)\n451:                (let [m (py/class-lookup o name)]\n452:                  (if (= m :py/missing)\n453:                    (if (= name \"__name__\") (py/str (get c :name)) (py/attr-error name))\n454:                    m))\n455:                (if (= t :list)\n456:                  (if (= name \"append\")\n457:                    (py/method o py.b/list-append)\n458:                    (py/attr-error name))\n459:                  (if (= t :function)\n460:                    (if (= name \"__name__\")\n461:                      (py/str (get c :name))\n462:                      (py/attr-error name))\n463:                    (if (= t :set)\n464:                      (if (= name \"add\") (py/method o py.b/set-add) (py/attr-error name))\n465:                      (if (= t :dict)\n466:                        (if (= name \"items\")\n467:                          (py/method o py.b/dict-items)\n468:                          (if (= name \"keys\")\n469:                            (py/method o py.